{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task SE-PE-01 requires implementing a `solve(case)` function that performs grammar-guided node reduction on a parse tree. Let me understand the requirements:\n\n1. **Input**: A `case` object with:\n   - `nodes`: list of nodes, each with `id`, `parent`, `symbol`, `depth`, `removable`, `utility`\n   - `required_symbols`: list of symbols that must remain represented\n\n2. **Output**: \n   - `removed_node_ids`: list of node IDs in removal order\n   - `retained_node_ids`: sorted list of retained node IDs\n\n3. **Rules**:\n   - Never remove the root (node with `parent: null`)\n   - Never remove a node with a required symbol (`removable: false` or symbol in `required_symbols`)\n   - Never remove a node if it would leave a retained child orphaned (never remove a node with retained children)\n   - Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented after removal\n   - Consider deeper nodes before shallower ones\n   - Use node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth\n   - Return sorted retained IDs and actual removal order\n\nLet me think about the algorithm:\n\n1. Build the tree structure\n2. Process nodes in order: deepest first, with node ID as tie-break at equal depth\n3. For each candidate node (removable), try to remove it:\n   - Check if removing it would leave any required symbols unrepresented\n   - Check if the node has any retained children (if so, can't remove it)\n   - If removal is valid, mark it as removed\n4. Return removed and retained lists\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Never remove a node with retained children.\" This means we check at the time of attempted removal whether the node still has children in the retained set.\n\nAlso: \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" This means we check after tentative removal whether all required symbols are still present in the retained set.\n\nThe ordering: \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes\" with \"Use node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth.\"\n\nSo we process nodes sorted by (depth descending, node_id ascending).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Build the node structure\n2. Sort candidates by (depth DESC, id ASC) - only considering removable nodes\n3. For each candidate in this order:\n   a. Check if any of its children are still retained (not removed)\n   b. If no retained children AND removing it would still keep all required symbols represented, remove it\n4. Track removal order and retained set\n\nLet me implement this:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case['nodes']\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\n    \n    # Build lookup structures\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n['id']: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n['parent'] is not None:\n            children[n['parent']].append(n['id'])\n    \n    # Track which nodes are retained\n    retained = set(n['id'] for n in nodes)\n    \n    # Get removable candidates sorted by depth DESC, then id ASC\n    candidates = [n for n in nodes if n['removable']]\n    candidates.sort(key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\n    \n    removed_order = []\n    \n    for node in candidates:\n        nid = node['id']\n        \n        # Check if node has any retained children\n        has_retained_children = any(child in retained for child in children[nid])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        \n        # Tentatively remove this node\n        retained.remove(nid)\n        \n        # Check if all required symbols are still represented\n        retained_symbols = set(node_map[r]['symbol'] for r in retained)\n        if required_symbols.issubset(retained_symbols):\n            # Valid removal - keep it removed\n            removed_order.append(nid)\n        else:\n            # Invalid - restore\n            retained.add(nid)\n    \n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        'removed_node_ids': removed_order,\n        'retained_node_ids': retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nLet me trace through case 000 to verify:\n\nNodes:\n- root: parent=null, symbol=root, depth=0, removable=false\n- n1: parent=root, symbol=s1, depth=1, removable=false\n- n2: parent=root, symbol=s2, depth=1, removable=true\n- n3: parent=root, symbol=s0, depth=1, removable=false\n- n4: parent=n2, symbol=s1, depth=2, removable=true\n- n5: parent=n3, symbol=s2, depth=2, removable=false\n- n6: parent=n1, symbol=s0, depth=2, removable=true\n\nrequired_symbols: {root, s1}\n\nChildren:\n- root: [n1, n2, n3]\n- n1: [n6]\n- n2: [n4]\n- n3: [n5]\n- n4: []\n- n5: []\n- n6: []\n\nRemovable candidates sorted by (depth DESC, id ASC):\n- Depth 2: n4, n6 (alphabetical: n4, n6)\n- Depth 1: n2\n\nProcessing order: n4, n6, n2\n\nInitial retained: {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, n6}\nRetained symbols: {root, s1, s2, s0}\nRequired: {root, s1}\n\n**n4** (depth=2, symbol=s1):\n- Children of n4: [] - no retained children\n- Remove n4 tentatively: retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n5, n6}\n- Retained symbols: {root, s1, s2, s0} (n1 has s1, still there)\n- Required symbols still present? Yes (root from root, s1 from n1)\n- Keep removed. removed_order = [n4]\n\n**n6** (depth=2, symbol=s0):\n- Children of n6: [] - no retained children\n- Remove n6 tentatively: retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n5}\n- Retained symbols: {root, s1, s2, s0} (n1=s1, n3=s0, etc.)\n- Required symbols still present? Yes\n- Keep removed. removed_order = [n4, n6]\n\n**n2** (depth=1, symbol=s2):\n- Children of n2: [n4] - n4 is removed, so not in retained. No retained children.\n- Remove n2 tentatively: retained = {root, n1, n3, n5}\n- Retained symbols: {root, s1, s0, s2} (root=root, n1=s1, n3=s0, n5=s2)\n- Required symbols still present? Yes\n- Keep removed. removed_order = [n4, n6, n2]\n\nFinal:\n- removed_node_ids: [n4, n6, n2]\n- retained_node_ids: sorted {root, n1, n3, n5} = [n1, n3, n5, root]... wait, string sorting: \"n1\" \u003c \"n3\" \u003c \"n5\" \u003c \"root\"\n\nsorted([\"root\", \"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\"]) in Python:\n- \"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\" (since 'n' \u003c 'r' in ASCII)\n\nSo retained_node_ids: [\"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\n\nThis seems correct. The algorithm looks good.\n\nNow let me format the Python code properly as a JSON string for the implementation field.\n\nThe Python code needs to be escaped properly:\n- newlines → \\n\n- backslashes → \\\\\n- quotes → \\\"\n\nLet me write the final JSON response:\n\n```json\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\\n    \\n    # Build lookup structures\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n['id']: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n['parent'] is not None:\\n            children[n['parent']].append(n['id'])\\n    \\n    # Track which nodes are retained\\n    retained = set(n['id'] for n in nodes)\\n    \\n    # Get removable candidates sorted by depth DESC, then id ASC\\n    candidates = [n for n in nodes if n['removable']]\\n    candidates.sort(key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    \\n    removed_order = []\\n    \\n    for node in candidates:\\n        nid = node['id']\\n        \\n        # Check if node has any retained children\\n        has_retained_children = any(child in retained for child in children[nid])\\n        if has_retained_children:\\n            continue\\n        \\n        # Tentatively remove this node\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        \\n        # Check if all required symbols are still represented\\n        retained_symbols = set(node_map[r]['symbol'] for r in retained)\\n        if required_symbols.issubset(retained_symbols):\\n            # Valid removal - keep it removed\\n            removed_order.append(nid)\\n        else:\\n            # Invalid - restore\\n            retained.add(nid)\\n    \\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\\n    \\n    return {\\n        'removed_node_ids': removed_order,\\n        'retained_node_ids': retained_sorted\\n    }\"}\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Let me double-check the JSON escaping.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\\n\\n    # Build lookup structures\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n['id']: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n['parent'] is not None:\\n            children[n['parent']].append(n['id'])\\n\\n    # All nodes start as retained\\n    retained = set(n['id'] for n in nodes)\\n\\n    # Removable candidates: process deepest first, tie-break by node ID ascending\\n    candidates = [n for n in nodes if n['removable']]\\n    candidates.sort(key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n\\n    removed_order = []\\n\\n    for node in candidates:\\n        nid = node['id']\\n\\n        # Cannot remove a node that still has retained children\\n        if any(child in retained for child in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Tentatively remove\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n\\n        # Verify all required symbols are still represented in the retained set\\n        retained_symbols = set(node_map[r]['symbol'] for r in retained)\\n        if required_symbols.issubset(retained_symbols):\\n            removed_order.append(nid)\\n        else:\\n            # Restore - removal would violate required symbol coverage\\n            retained.add(nid)\\n\\n    return {\\n        'removed_node_ids': removed_order,\\n        'retained_node_ids': sorted(retained)\\n    }\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01vNirAx1VaAHe6rCkh9702U","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2408},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2408,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":52,"output_tokens":2769,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2378},"service_tier":"standard"}}